# LotSync .gitignore
#
# Principle: source, documentation, migrations, tests, and synthetic
# fixtures are always tracked. Anything generated, local-machine-
# specific, or containing real dealership data is never tracked --
# see ARCHITECTURE.md / PRODUCT.md on why real customer exports never
# belong in this repo (tests/fixtures/README.md: synthetic data only,
# checked in on purpose; real exports are not).

# --- Python build/runtime artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Test / type-checker caches ---
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# --- IDE / editor ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Claude Code local settings (personal/machine-specific; see
# .claude/settings.json if a shared version is ever added) ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Local persistence (Phase 2) ---
# SQLite database files -- local state only, never a source artifact.
# See database/migrations/ for the actual versioned schema (tracked).
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Runtime data directories ---
# data/uploads/ holds real dealership export files (Keyper, Tekion,
# MDD, RecovR, RapidRecon, oms_config.xlsx) at runtime -- never checked
# in; these are live customer data, not test fixtures. See
# tests/fixtures/synthetic/ (tracked, below) for the checked-in
# equivalent used by the test suite.
data/uploads/*
!data/uploads/.gitkeep

# data/outputs/ holds generated CSV reports -- reproducible output,
# not source.
data/outputs/*
!data/outputs/.gitkeep

# data/api_uploads/ (Phase 3, Sprint 4) -- one subfolder per
# POST /inventory-sync/run request, holding that request's uploaded
# report files. Same reasoning as data/uploads/ above: live dealership
# data at runtime, never checked in. Kept entirely separate from
# data/uploads/ so the CLI (main.py, find_upload()) and API upload
# workflows never collide -- see sync/pipeline.py.
data/api_uploads/*
!data/api_uploads/.gitkeep

# --- Developer tooling runtime state ---
# tools/.state/ holds generated run-*.ps1 wrapper scripts, *.pid files,
# and *.log output from tools/launch.ps1 -- machine-local runtime state,
# not source. See tools/README.md.
tools/.state/

# --- Explicitly NOT ignored (documented for clarity, no pattern needed) ---
# tests/fixtures/synthetic/ -- synthetic, checked-in test data, always tracked
# database/migrations/ -- versioned schema, always tracked
# *.md -- all documentation, always tracked
